strictly increasing, then ${f}^{′}(x)>0.$\n\n- If $f(x)$ is strictly decreasing, then ${f}^{′}(x)<0.$\n\nThe information about ${f}^{′}(x)$ can be summarized in the following table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & (-\\infty ,0) & 0 & (0,2) & 2 & (2,\\infty ) \\\\ f & ↗ & \\text{max} & ↘ & \\text{min} & ↗ \\\\ {f}^{′} & + & 0 & - & 0 & +\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{′}(x)<0$ on the interval $(0,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014428/state.json" "file_sha256" "063712de5aec34643d50968e6bdee7f1fa61ab590844c7c8b87cf01c3ddf9379"} {"question" "q-18227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014428/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "459e3f05c236391edd9c7055cd83c3237fce91edab856e4b2d53085e190b86a0"} {"question" "q-18227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014428/state.json" "file_sha256" "063712de5aec34643d50968e6bdee7f1fa61ab590844c7c8b87cf01c3ddf9379"} {"question" "q-18227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(0,2)"] ["text" "$(-\\infty ,0)$ and $(2,\\infty )$ only"] ["text" "$(-\\infty ,0)$ only"] ["text" "$(2,\\infty )$ only"] ["text" "No interval exists where ${f}^{′}(x)<0$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014428/state.json" "file_sha256" "063712de5aec34643d50968e6bdee7f1fa61ab590844c7c8b87cf01c3ddf9379"} {"question" "q-18227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(0,2)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014428/state.json" "fil